Q: prevent resize column from shrinking other columns A: <p>Create an outer table that has however many rows you need and each row has just one &lt;td&gt;&lt;/td&gt; with width set to 100% and overflow hidden, then inside each of these tds/rows insert a new table where you can add as many columns as you wish and each column can be as wide as you wish.</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>table {
  border-collapse: collapse;
  overflow: hidden;
  width: 700px;
}

table td {
  overflow: hidden;
  border: solid #000 2px; /*for visual*/
}

.pad0 {
  padding: 0;
}

.pad5 {
  padding: 5px
}

.pad10 {
  padding: 10px;
}

.txtleft {
  text-align: left;
}

.txtcenter {
  text-align: center;
}

.txtright {
  text-align: right;
}

.wid10 {
  width: 10%;
}

.wid20 {
  width: 20%;
}

.wid30 {
  width: 30%;
}

.wid40 {
  width: 40%;
}

.wid50 {
  width: 50%;
}

.wid60 {
  width: 60%;
}

.wid70 {
  width: 70%;
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;table&gt;
  &lt;tr&gt;
    &lt;td&gt;
      &lt;table class="wid100"&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
          &lt;td class="wid40 txtright"&gt;
          &lt;/td&gt;

          &lt;td class="wid60 txtleft"&gt;
          &lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
      &lt;/table&gt;
    &lt;/td&gt;
  &lt;/tr&gt;

  &lt;tr&gt;
    &lt;td&gt;
      &lt;table class="wid100"&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
          &lt;td class="wid10 txtright"&gt;
          &lt;/td&gt;

          &lt;td class="wid40 txtcenter"&gt;
          &lt;/td&gt;

          &lt;td class="wid30 txtleft"&gt;
          &lt;/td&gt;

          &lt;td class="wid10 txtcenter"&gt;
          &lt;/td&gt;

          &lt;td class="wid10 txtright"&gt;
          &lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
      &lt;/table&gt;
    &lt;/td&gt;
  &lt;/tr&gt;

  &lt;tr&gt;
    &lt;td&gt;
      &lt;table class="wid100"&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
          &lt;td class="wid40 txtcenter"&gt;
          &lt;/td&gt;

          &lt;td class="wid30 txtcenter"&gt;
          &lt;/td&gt;

          &lt;td class="wid20 txtright"&gt;
          &lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
      &lt;/table&gt;
    &lt;/td&gt;
  &lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
